    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and verified. Everything wired up correctly:\n\n- **`title`** is mapped from the request DTO into the `Owner` entity (`owner.setTitle(...)`), persisted, and returned.\n- **`salutation`** is composed on read as `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is present.\n\n## Summary of changes\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (optional input, `MR|MRS|MS|DR`) to the `OwnerFields` schema and a read-only derived `salutation` to the `Owner` schema. These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` getters/setters.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `salutation`: `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, otherwise just `lastName`. (`title` itself maps automatically by name.)\n\n4. **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table.\n\n5. **Seed data SQL** (`hsqldb`, `mysql`) \u2014 updated the positional `INSERT`s to include a `NULL` title (h2/postgres use named-column inserts and needed no change).\n\n## Test results\n\nThe full suite builds and passes \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` which asserts `$.salutation == \"DR who\"`. `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class in the project.",
